{"nodes": [{"id": "raw_architectural_debt_2026_08_02_table", "label": "Architectural Debt Register (2026-08-02)", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "raw/architectural-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "raw_architectural_debt_2026_08_02_ad_1", "label": "AD-1 (HIGH): Implicit-SQ promotion triplicated", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "raw/architectural-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "fromPart10 trusts the parser's el.items; fromPart10Stream hand-rolls an FFFE peek; decodeCore.classifyElement does neither. Interest: the lazy core silently diverges from eager for defined-length unknown-implicit elements whose value starts with an item tag \u2014 three behaviors where the architecture promises one. Principal: make decodeCore peek-aware; delete both duplicates. Flagged 'highest value' by the repo's own final review."}, {"id": "raw_architectural_debt_2026_08_02_ad_2", "label": "AD-2 (HIGH): Legacy island \u2014 AsyncDicomReader (774 loc)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "raw/architectural-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "AsyncDicomReader runs its own header/element loop on the old listener vocabulary; never touches the event-stream contract. Interest: two read paths to maintain and test; frame-level pixel semantics live only here; every contract improvement bypasses it. Principal: K7 re-platform \u2014 per-frame events in fromPart10Stream or frame assembly in a shim. Assessed, costed, deferred to 1.x in writing."}, {"id": "raw_architectural_debt_2026_08_02_ad_3", "label": "AD-3 (MED): Dual read cores \u2014 DCMJS_CORE=eager escape hatch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "raw/architectural-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The eager loop (DicomMessage._read) is kept as the DCMJS_CORE=eager escape hatch. Interest: every change runs the full suite twice; the R7 deletion list is blocked; AsyncDicomReader depends on _read for its meta group. Principal: delete after AD-2 lands and the beta soaks \u2014 order of operations already specified in the roadmap."}, {"id": "raw_architectural_debt_2026_08_02_ad_4", "label": "AD-4 (MED): Circular coupling \u2014 DicomMessage \u21c4 LazyDicomReader + setter injection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "raw/architectural-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DicomMessage \u21c4 LazyDicomReader import cycle, plus the setDicomMessageClass / setTagClass setter injection in index.js. Interest: import cycles constrain packaging; the module graph can't be layered cleanly at the bottom. Principal: the 1.x package split (data / dictionary / streaming / features) makes the setters unnecessary \u2014 already on the backlog."}, {"id": "raw_architectural_debt_2026_08_02_ad_5", "label": "AD-5 (LOW): Streaming source imports the legacy reader", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "raw/architectural-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "fromPart10Stream imports DicomMessage for error/compat parity. Interest: a thread from the new world into the old; complicates eventual eager deletion. Principal: falls out of AD-3's deletion list; verify when the eager loop goes."}], "edges": [{"source": "raw_architectural_debt_2026_08_02_table", "target": "raw_architectural_debt_2026_08_02_ad_1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "raw/architectural-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location